  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would provide an&nbsp;insufficient internal quality of accommodation especially for the first and second floor flats, poor layout between the flats would could result in noise disturbances and a lack of external amenity space provided for the second floor flat. As a result, it is considered to represent a poor quality of accommodation and as such be deemed as unacceptable and contrary to:DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)&nbsp;Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies BP5 and BP6 of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Part 6 in Policy DMNE1&nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposed development fails to provide sufficient quantum&nbsp;of cycle and refuse storage which would be well located and suitable for use for the three separate flats. As such the proposed development is considered to unacceptable and contrary to:Paragraphs 104 and 106 of the National Planning Policy Framework (Decemeber 2023)Policy T5 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy BR11 of&nbsp;&nbsp;the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policy DMT3 and&nbsp;Part 3 in Policy DMSI 8&nbsp;of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)The Council&#39;s Planning Advice Note on Waste and Recycling Provisions in New and Refurbished Residential Developments (2021)"
  ],
